      <NOTES
        |Imprint the Spectral profile of one sound to another.
        |
        |1. Load the "ReaFir" FX on the item you want to use as the source. 
        |
        |2. Mode: Substract – enable "automatically build noise profile"
        |
        |3. Play the sound until the filter changes gets the spectral profile.
        |
        |5. Perhaps put the whole filter graph up a few decibels (to avoid being too quiet) 
        |with holding cmd and dragging the curve up. 
        |
        |6. Safe this (the "+" sign in the upper right area) to a new preset.
        |
        |5. You can now load this preset to other instances of ReaFir
        |
        |6. Load ReaFir unto another sound, select your saved preset, and change the mode to EQ
